    "result_text": "All 275 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created without a registration date, it now defaults to today's date and is returned in the owner response as `registrationDate` in ISO format (`YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java` (model)** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` field (`LocalDate`) mapped to a new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields`, the field flows into both the request DTO (so a caller *may* supply one) and the response DTO. The MapStruct mapper picks it up automatically by name.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after mapping the request, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the caller didn't provide one, before persisting.\n\n4. **Database schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table so the new field persists across all supported databases (tests run against hsqldb).\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`** \u2014 added two tests: one asserting the default is today's date when omitted, and one asserting a supplied `registrationDate` is preserved.\n\nExisting behavior is untouched \u2014 the field is optional, so validation and duplicate-detection tests still pass.",
